  <prompt>Three closed follow-ups to 089c. Read notes/089-assignment-override-service.md, section "089c": "Decisions and deviations", "STOP: stale base-code Signals (POML)" and the two review subsections. Nothing else is in scope.</prompt>

  <goal>
    1. A record-level rule change (`ChangeRuleCoreAsync`) closes, after its commit and best effort, the open Signals the BASE rule raised on the In Review invoices filed directly on that record, as Superseded, through the existing SignalClosureService / SignalWriter close. (Correction, 089e pass 1 F3: the close does not record the record rule's version; the writer stores the resolution only.) The response says whether the close completed, what it covered (the record's own invoices only, pass 1 F2), and how many of those invoices the caller can see.
    2. A rule-set by-id route answers a record-scoped set with 409 and a new stable code (`ruleset.record_scoped`), a message naming the override routes and the record kind, logged under the code, ONLY when the caller passes the route's existing Read check on the set or its core record. A caller without that Read still gets the uniform 404. Firm-facing readers (`GetFirmClauseAsync` and any external path) keep hiding record-scoped sets.
    3. The Billing Administrator role source holds every privilege the change and removal routes check, at the depth each check needs, with file:line evidence for every check. Anything missing is added to the role SOURCE only, with the guard test updated.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Procedures/ProcedureAssignmentService.cs (ChangeRuleAsync / ChangeRuleCoreAsync; RuleChangedView)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/ProcedureAssignmentEndpoints.cs (pass the caller token to the change)</file>
