    <reference-implementation>
      Item 1: `ProcedureAssignmentService.RemoveAsync`, the close after the commit: the change stays committed, a close fault is counted, `closeComplete` and a message say what happened, and `AffectedInvoiceCounter.CountVisibleOpenInvoicesAsync` counts the caller-visible invoices. The selection is `SignalClosureService.SelectOpenSignalsOfPolicyAsync` (ProcedureRetireSelectionGuardTests: nothing under Services/Finance/Procedures queries `sprk_signal` directly). Item 2: `RequireReadOnTheOverridesSubject` (Refused = the same bytes as a missing row). Item 3: `scripts/ebilling/Deploy-EbillingBillingAdminRole.ps1` and `RuleSetRolePrivilegeGuardTests`.
    </reference-implementation>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner 2026-11-04">Item 1 is option (b): Superseded, through the existing close path. No new Signal selection, no new Signal writer.</constraint>
    <constraint source="089c">Item 1 must-not-fire: Signals of other records, of other rules, of another firm's invoices for a firm-scoped change, and on invoices that are not In Review stay untouched. The count covers only invoices the caller can Read.</constraint>
    <constraint source="089c deviation 1">Item 2: no new existence oracle. A caller without the route's Read gets bytes identical to a missing id. If no by-id route already checks Read on the set or on its core record, STOP item 2 and report the options; do not invent a new auth check here.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-123">Item 3: never Global, never Deep held in the root. If a needed depth would reach the Secure Record unit, STOP.</constraint>
    <constraint source="live changes">No live write. A role change is source only; applying it needs the owner's go in the main session and notices to uac-r2 and ontology-r1.</constraint>
    <constraint source="parallel">082 may edit RuleSetService; keep the change there small.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Item 1 must-fire: an open base-rule Signal on an In Review invoice of this record is Resolved/Superseded after a change. (Corrected, pass 1 F3: the close names no version; none is stored.)</criterion>
    <criterion>Item 1 must-not-fire: another record's invoice, another rule's Signal, a Pending or closed invoice, and (firm-scoped change) another firm's invoice keep their Signals open.</criterion>
    <criterion>Item 1 fault: a close fault leaves the change committed (201, record rule in force) and answers `closeComplete=false` with a message.</criterion>
    <criterion>Item 1: the response count is the caller-visible count; an unreadable invoice is not counted.</criterion>
    <criterion>Item 2: either the 409 with code and body for a reader, a byte-identical 404 for a non-reader, unchanged firm and external paths and one seed proof; or a recorded STOP with the evidence and options.</criterion>
    <criterion>Item 3: the privilege list (privilege, depth needed, depth held, file:line of each check) is in the notes; any addition is in the role source with the guard updated; the dev state is reported read-only when it differs.</criterion>
    <criterion>Each behaviour change has a test that fails before it and passes after (seed proof recorded).</criterion>
    <criterion>Gates: build 0 errors; unit filter `ProcedureAssignment|RuleSetService|SignalClosure|Signal`; ArchTests `RouteAuthorizationGuard|RecordOwnerAssignmentCensus|ProcedureRolePrivilege|FinanceStepZero`; publish size against a fresh master; code-review and adr-check.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
